ESP-IDF v5.5.5, components/esp_system: on an ESP32-P4 before revision 3
(CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3), internal data has two regions, and the
dram0_data and dram0_bss placements are made in both, with the link using
--enable-non-contiguous-regions -- so one library's .data or .bss can be split
between them. esp-vim restores Vim's .data and zeroes its .bss between bounds
made with SURROUND, which a split breaks: each bound is assigned twice and
covers one part.

This adds a target to each high-region section, dram1_data and dram1_bss, that
appears nowhere else: a placement there is made once, whole. No mapping uses
them unless a fragment asks (esp-vim's components/vim/linker.lf, on those
chips), so nothing else moves.

--- a/ld/ld.dram.sections
+++ b/ld/ld.dram.sections
@@ -96,6 +96,10 @@
     mapping[dram0_data]
     mutable[dram0_data]
 
+    /* esp-vim: a target only this region has, for data that must not be
+       split between the two regions (esp-vim's linker.lf). */
+    mapping[dram1_data]
+
     _data_end_high = ABSOLUTE(.);
   } > dram_high_seg
 
@@ -106,6 +110,9 @@
     mapping[dram0_bss]
     mutable[dram0_bss]
 
+    /* esp-vim: as dram1_data. */
+    mapping[dram1_bss]
+
     ALIGNED_SYMBOL(8, _bss_end_high)
   } > dram_high_seg
 
